h key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise children come in the order they were first added.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" links, and the edge labels are slices of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"buffer of symbols, so the tree holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1 vertices and label symbols, and copying"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/PrefixView"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/init()","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/init(_:)"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/count","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/isEmpty"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/contains(_:)-39nls","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/elements(withPrefix:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/hasPrefix(_:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/insert(_:)-3ywij","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/longestPrefix(of:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree\/remove(